      "layout": "standardStudy",
      "translation": "To use",
      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: nutzen most often means to use something for a practical purpose.",
        "It can also mean useful when asking if something is beneficial.",
        "To use everyday is often benutzen, but nutzen emphasizes benefit or purpose more.",
        "The phrase die Chance nutzen means to seise the opportunity.",
        "The context shows whether it is a use or a benefit."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Ich nutze die Zeit zum Lernen.",
          "lv": "I use the time to study."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir nutzen diese Chance.",
          "lv": "We take advantage of this opportunity."
        },
        {
          "de": "Das nutzt mir nichts.",
          "lv": "It does me no good."
        },
        {
          "de": "Viele Leute nutzen das Internet.",
          "lv": "Many people use the internet."
        },
        {
          "de": "Kann ich dein Fahrrad benutzen?",
          "lv": "Can i use your bike"
        }
      ],
